#: manual/about.md:3
msgid "This collection gathers the *Probably Stolen* mods written by KCN-judu. Every mod lives in its own repository, with its own releases and Steam Workshop page; the collection repository ties them together as Git submodules and builds this site from their documentation."
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:5
#: manual/contribute/documentation_standard.md:5
msgid "Principles"
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:7
msgid "**Keep the game's rules.** A mod may remove waiting, guessing or wasted work, but customers accept what they accepted before, locks still lock, and saves load as they did. Where a mod changes how something is computed, it computes the same answer."
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:9
msgid "**Ask for nothing.** Every mod declares no capabilities, so the game enables it without a permission prompt. Reflection only names game types directly, which the game's mod scanner accepts."
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:11
msgid "**Fail quietly.** A patch that cannot attach, after a game update for example, turns its own feature off and writes one line to `Player.log`. It never stops the rest of the mod or the game."
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:13
msgid "**Measure first.** Performance work starts from the game's own log and from a profiler, not from guesses. The numbers behind each fix are in its documentation."
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:15
msgid "The mods"
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:17
msgid "Mod"
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:17
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:19
msgid "Demand Highlight"
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:19
msgid "Outlines what the customer at the counter wants, and marks your stock by type with the Item Filter."
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:20
msgid "Quick Call"
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:20
msgid "Calls go straight to the choices."
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:21
msgid "Save Language Converter"
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:21
msgid "Converts a copy of a save started in another language."
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:22
msgid "Performance Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:22
msgid "Removes stutters with large, packed storage."
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:23
msgid "Window Workspaces"
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:23
msgid "Snaps windows together and switches whole sets of them with one key."
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:24
msgid "Better Key Bindings"
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:24
msgid "Key combinations and extra mouse buttons for every key binding."
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:26
msgid "Look"
msgstr ""

#: manual/about.md:28
msgid "The site and the mod covers share one design: the game's dusk-violet windows, cream text and teal title bars, square panels with a one-pixel bevel, and pixel lettering for names and labels. The cover system is described in `design/DESIGN.md` of the collection repository. Chinese headings use Cubic 11, an open-source pixel font released under the SIL Open Font License."
msgstr ""

